Project Description

This project contains all research materials, datasets, and documentation related to the paper titled “A Multi-Model Hybrid Convolutional Framework (MMH-CNN) for Efficient Event Detection in Wireless Sensor Networks.”
The research focuses on developing and evaluating a novel hybrid deep learning model that integrates multiple lightweight CNN architectures (HST-CNN, Tiny-CNN, and MobileNet) to enhance event detection accuracy and reduce computational cost in resource-constrained Wireless Sensor Networks (WSNs).

The repository includes:

Complete research paper draft (in Word and PDF formats)

Model architecture design and training configurations

Dataset details (Intel Berkeley Lab and SensorScope WSN datasets)

Experimental results, performance comparisons, and plots

Supporting references and literature review documents

This project serves as a collaborative workspace for the research team to review, modify, and enhance the MMH-CNN framework for future journal submission and model deployment in real-time WSN environments
